/-!
# Flat base change for the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme

Let `q : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes and `I : Y.IdealSheafData` a quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals on `Y`. Two parallel towers in this repository describe the same mathematics and never
meet. On one side the ideal sheaf is a `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, whose inverse
image is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap`, and which is where local principality
([Stacks, Tag 01WR]) and the Fitting-ideal stalk criteria live. On the other side it is a
submodule of the structure sheaf, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule`, which
is where the generation and finiteness properties of `X.Modules` live — `IsGeneratedByNear`,
`SheafOfModules.IsCardinalGenerated`, and the descent statements of [Stacks, Tag 082U]. The
passage between the two towers already exists in both directions
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule` and
`Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafDataOfSubmodule`); what did not exist anywhere in the tree is the
**compatibility of that passage with pullback**, and this file supplies it:

`q^* (I ⊆ 𝒪_Y) ≅ (I·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X)` for flat `q`,

that is, `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealFlatIso`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackSect`: the pullback of a section of a module over an open of
  the target, restricted to an open of the source, written at the `Γ(·, ·)` spelling.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.idealIota`: the inclusion `I ⟶ 𝒪_Y` of the ideal sheaf, named at the
  `Y.Modules` spelling.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealMap`: the canonical map `q^* I ⟶ 𝒪_X`, the pullback of
  the inclusion followed by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealComparison`: its factorisation through the ideal sheaf of
  `I.comap q`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealFlatIso`: **the comparison.** For flat `q` the
  factorisation is an isomorphism `q^* I ≅ I.comap q`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.mem_submodule_of_one_tmul`: a map out of an extension of scalars takes
  its values in a submodule as soon as its values on the pure tensors `1 ⊗ m` do.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.mem_span_range_pullbackSect`: over a pair of affine charts the sections
  of a pullback are spanned by the pullbacks of sections.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealMap_app_pullbackSect`: the canonical map sends the
  pullback of a section `a` of `I` to its image `q.appLE U V (a)` under `q`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealMap_app_mem` and
  `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.exists_app_eq_of_mem`: over a pair of affine charts the image of the
  canonical map on sections is **exactly** the ideal that `I.comap q` cuts out.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.mono_pullbackIdealComparison`,
  `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.epi_pullbackIdealComparison`,
  `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.isIso_pullbackIdealComparison`: monomorphy (from flatness), epimorphy
  (unconditional) and hence invertibility of the comparison.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealFlatIso_hom_comp_iota`: the comparison is compatible with
  the two inclusions into the structure sheaves, which is what identifies it.

## Implementation notes

**Why flatness, and where it is used.** Epimorphy of the comparison is unconditional: it is the
statement that the ideal `(I.comap q)(V)` cut out on an affine open `V` of the source lying over
an affine open `U` of the target is generated by the images of the sections of `I` over `U`,
which is `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`. Flatness enters only through monomorphy: the
inclusion `I ⟶ 𝒪_Y` is a monomorphism and `q^*` preserves monomorphisms when `q` is flat
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.mono_pullback_map_of_flat`, which is [Stacks, Tag 02N4] on
stalks). Without flatness the comparison is still an epimorphism onto the inverse-image ideal
sheaf — the `q^*I ⟶ 𝒪_X` of a non-flat `q` genuinely has a kernel — so the hypothesis is not an
artefact of the proof. No hypothesis beyond flatness is needed, and in particular neither
finiteness of `I` nor quasi-compactness of `q` appears.

**Why the sections of `q^*I` are computable at all.** Both halves of the image computation rest
on `AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso`, the identification
`Γ(X, V) ⊗_{Γ(Y, U)} Γ(F, U) ≅ Γ(q^* F, V)` for a quasi-coherent `F` and a compatible pair of
affine opens, normalised on `1 ⊗ a` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso_one_tmul`. Transporting a statement about
*all* sections of `q^* F` across it needs the pure tensors `1 ⊗ a` to generate, and that is
`Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.mem_submodule_of_one_tmul`, proved not by induction on the tensor
product but by `ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.hom_ext` applied to the quotient by the submodule: the
two maps `q^*F ⟶ (target)/p` agreeing on the pure tensors are equal, which is exactly the
statement that every section lands in `p`. The induction is unavailable in practice because
`ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.obj'` is a `def` and not an `abbrev`, so the goals that
`TensorProduct.induction_on` produces are not type-correct at the transparency `rw` builds its
motive at.

**Which submodule.** "The ideal sheaf of `I`, as a submodule of `𝒪_X`" is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule`, and the reason this file can be written
at it is that its sections over an affine open are identified with `I.ideal U` *on the nose*
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule_obj_affine`); that identification is what
both halves of the image computation consume. Writing it instead at the `I ^ 1 • 𝒪_X` spelling
of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower.idealPowerMultiple` would record the affine sections only
as `I(U) ^ 1 • ⊤`, and the step from there to `I(U)` is a real obstruction: the module
`Γ(𝒪_Y, U)` does not carry its ring structure at that spelling, so `⊤` contains no `1` to
multiply by. The obstruction is *routed around* rather than solved —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.idealPowerMultiple_one_eq_unitSubmodule` identifies
the two, so no ring structure ever has to be transported onto `Γ(𝒪_Y, U)`.

**Section-level spellings.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection` lands in
`((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj F).val.obj (op V)`, the `ModuleCat`-valued presheaf, while the
module instance `Module Γ(X, V) Γ(M, V)` that `Submodule.span` needs is declared at the
`AddCommGrpCat`-valued `Γ(·, ·)`. `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackSect` is the same term written
at the second spelling; the two are definitionally equal, and naming the ascription is what
keeps every intermediate `Submodule` goal type-correct. The same discipline is why
`Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.idealIota` exists.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02N4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02N4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 082U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/082U)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite TopologicalSpace
open scoped ChangeOfRings

universe u

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Algebraization.monoSubmoduleι
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓ Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsModuleΓSheaf
  Stacks.Algebraization.sectionsSMulCommClassΓ

namespace Stacks.ClosedSubscheme

/-! ### Values of a map out of an extension of scalars -/

/-- **A map out of an extension of scalars takes its values in a submodule as soon as its values
on the pure tensors `1 ⊗ m` do.** The two morphisms `S ⊗_R M ⟶ N ⧸ p` given by the composite
with the quotient map and by zero agree on the pure tensors `1 ⊗ m`, hence are equal by
`ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.hom_ext`; that equality, read on an element, is the assertion. -/
theorem mem_submodule_of_one_tmul {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) (M : ModuleCat.{u} R) {N : Type u} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N]
    (g : (ModuleCat.extendScalars f).obj M ⟶ ModuleCat.of S N) (p : Submodule S N)
    (h : ∀ m : M, g ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R, f] m) ∈ p)
    (z : (ModuleCat.extendScalars f).obj M) : g z ∈ p := by
  have key : g ≫ ModuleCat.ofHom p.mkQ = 0 := by
    refine ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.hom_ext fun m => ?_
    have h0 : p.mkQ ((ConcreteCategory.hom g) ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R, f] m)) = 0 :=
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero p).2 (h m)
    exact h0
  have hz := congrArg (fun φ : (ModuleCat.extendScalars f).obj M ⟶ ModuleCat.of S (N ⧸ p) =>
    ConcreteCategory.hom φ z) key
  simpa [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] using hz

/-! ### Pullbacks of sections -/

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (q : X ⟶ Y)

/-- **The pullback of a section**, at the `Γ(·, ·)` spelling: a section of `F` over an open `U`
of the target becomes, through the unit of `q^* ⊣ q_*`, a section of `q^* F` over `q⁻¹U`, and is
restricted here to an open `V ≤ q⁻¹U`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection` written at the `AddCommGrpCat`-valued
presheaf, which is the spelling at which the module structure on sections is declared. -/
abbrev pullbackSect (F : Y.Modules) (U : Y.Opens) (V : X.Opens) (h : V ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (a : Γ(F, U)) : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj F, V) :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj F).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op
    (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction q).unit.app F).app U a)

/-- **Over a pair of affine charts the sections of a pullback are spanned by the pullbacks of
sections.** Every section of `q^* F` over `V` is the image under
`AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso` of an element of
`Γ(X, V) ⊗_{Γ(Y, U)} Γ(F, U)`, and that isomorphism takes `1 ⊗ a` to the pullback of `a`. -/
theorem mem_span_range_pullbackSect (F : Y.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    {U : Y.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {V : X.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    (hVU : V ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ U) (t : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj F, V)) :
    t ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, V) (Set.range (pullbackSect q F U V hVU)) := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso q F hU hV hVU).hom).surjective t
  subst hz
  refine mem_submodule_of_one_tmul (q.appLE U V hVU).hom (ModuleCat.of Γ(Y, U) Γ(F, U))
    (affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso q F hU hV hVU).hom _ (fun a => ?_) z
  rw [affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso_one_tmul]
  exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩

/-! ### Two locality statements -/

/-- **Membership in a submodule of a sheaf of modules is local**, for an arbitrary cover: if
every point of `W` has a neighbourhood in `W` on which `t` restricts into `N`, then `t` is
already a section of `N` over `W`.

This is `Stacks.Algebraization.mem_submodule_of_affine` with the affine basis replaced by an
arbitrary choice of neighbourhoods, which is what lets a cover be chosen compatibly with a cover
of the target. -/
theorem mem_submodule_of_cover {F : X.Modules} (N : F.Submodule) (W : X.Opens) (t : Γ(F, W))
    (h : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ (V : X.Opens) (_ : x ∈ V) (hVW : V ≤ W),
      F.val.map (homOfLE hVW).op t ∈ N.toSubmodule.obj (op V)) :
    t ∈ N.toSubmodule.obj (op W) := by
  apply N.isSheaf
  rw [Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, hVW, hmem⟩ := h x hx
  exact ⟨V, homOfLE hVW, hmem, hxV⟩

/-- **A compatible pair of affine charts around a point.** Every point of an open `W` of the
source has an affine neighbourhood inside `W` which lies over an affine open of the target. The
affine opens form a basis on both schemes, so one chooses the chart on the target first and then
refines inside its preimage. -/
theorem exists_affine_chart_pair (W : X.Opens) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ W) :
    ∃ (U : Y.affineOpens) (V : X.affineOpens) (_ : (V : X.Opens) ≤ W),
      x ∈ (V : X.Opens) ∧ (V : X.Opens) ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ (U : Y.Opens) := by
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hqxU, -⟩ :=
    Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp Y.isBasis_affineOpens (U := ⊤) (x := q.base x) trivial
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, hVW⟩ := Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens
    (U := W ⊓ q ⁻¹ᵁ U) (x := x) ⟨hx, hqxU⟩
  exact ⟨⟨U, hU⟩, ⟨V, hV⟩, le_trans hVW inf_le_left, hxV, le_trans hVW inf_le_right⟩

/-! ### The canonical map `q^* I ⟶ 𝒪_X` -/

variable (I : Y.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The inclusion of the ideal sheaf into the structure sheaf**, named at the `Y.Modules`
spelling so that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.Hom.app` applies to it. -/
abbrev idealIota : (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) ⟶ Scheme.unitModule Y :=
  I.unitSubmodule.ι

/-- **The canonical map `q^* I ⟶ 𝒪_X`**: the pullback of the inclusion of the ideal sheaf,
followed by the identification of the pullback of the structure sheaf of the target with the
structure sheaf of the source. -/
def pullbackIdealMap :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) ⟶
      Scheme.unitModule X :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullback q).map (idealIota I) ≫ (Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso q).hom

/-- **The structure-sheaf comparison, read on a pulled-back section.** The identification
`q^* 𝒪_Y ≅ 𝒪_X` carries the pullback of a function on `U` to its image under `q`, restricted. -/
theorem pullbackUnitIso_hom_app_pullbackSect (U : Y.Opens) (V : X.Opens) (h : V ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (b : Γ(Scheme.unitModule Y, U)) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso q).hom.app V (pullbackSect q (Scheme.unitModule Y) U V h b) =
      q.appLE U V h b := by
  have hnat := Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_presheaf_map (Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso q).hom
    (homOfLE h) (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction q).unit.app
      (Scheme.unitModule Y)).app U b)
  have hu := Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso_homEquiv q
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit] at hu
  have hb : (Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso q).hom.app (q ⁻¹ᵁ U)
      (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction q).unit.app
        (Scheme.unitModule Y)).app U b) = q.app U b :=
    congrArg (fun t : Scheme.unitModule Y ⟶
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward q).obj (Scheme.unitModule X) =>
      Scheme.Modules.Hom.app t U b) hu
  rw [hnat, hb]
  rfl

/-- **The canonical map, read on a pulled-back section.** It sends the pullback of a section `a`
of the ideal sheaf over `U` to the image of `a` under `q`, restricted to `V`. -/
theorem pullbackIdealMap_app_pullbackSect (U : Y.Opens) (V : X.Opens) (h : V ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (a : Γ((I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules), U)) :
    (pullbackIdealMap q I).app V
        (pullbackSect q (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) U V h a) =
      q.appLE U V h (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (idealIota I) U a) := by
  rw [pullbackIdealMap, Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app]
  have hnat := Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection_naturality q (idealIota I) U V h a
  exact Eq.trans (congrArg ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackUnitIso q).hom.app V) hnat)
    (pullbackUnitIso_hom_app_pullbackSect q U V h (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (idealIota I) U a))

/-- **An ideal sheaf is quasi-coherent**, in the form instance search needs in order to apply
`Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.mem_span_range_pullbackSect` to it. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_unitSubmoduleSheaf :
    ((I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules)).IsQuasicoherent :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule_isQuasicoherent I

/-! ### The image of the canonical map on an affine chart -/

/-- The sections of the inverse-image ideal sheaf over an affine chart are the extended ideal. -/
private theorem comap_unitSubmodule_obj_eq_map (U : Y.affineOpens) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (hVU : (V : X.Opens) ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ (U : Y.Opens)) :
    ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) =
      Ideal.map (q.appLE U.1 V.1 hVU).hom (I.ideal U) := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule_obj_affine,
    Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE I q U V hVU]

/-- The map on sections over `V` of a morphism of modules, as a linear map. -/
private def appLinear {F G : X.Modules} (φ : F ⟶ G) (V : X.Opens) :
    Γ(F, V) →ₗ[Γ(X, V)] Γ(G, V) where
  toFun := Scheme.Modules.Hom.app φ V
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' := Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul φ

/-- **The canonical map lands in the inverse-image ideal sheaf, over a pair of affine charts.**
The sections of `q^* I` over `V` are spanned by the pullbacks of the sections of `I` over `U`,
and those are carried into `(I.comap q)(V)` by
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`. -/
theorem pullbackIdealMap_app_mem (U : Y.affineOpens) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (hVU : (V : X.Opens) ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ (U : Y.Opens))
    (s : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj
      (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules), V.1)) :
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (pullbackIdealMap q I) V.1 s ∈
      ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) := by
  refine (Submodule.span_le (p := (((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1)).comap
    (appLinear (pullbackIdealMap q I) V.1))).2 ?_
    (mem_span_range_pullbackSect q (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules)
      U.2 V.2 hVU s)
  rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
  have ha : Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (idealIota I) U.1 a ∈
      I.unitSubmodule.toSubmodule.obj (op U.1) := a.2
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule_obj_affine] at ha
  have h : Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (pullbackIdealMap q I) V.1
      (pullbackSect q (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) U.1 V.1 hVU a) ∈
      ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1) := by
    rw [pullbackIdealMap_app_pullbackSect, comap_unitSubmodule_obj_eq_map q I U V hVU]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (q.appLE U.1 V.1 hVU).hom (show (_ : Γ(Y, U.1)) ∈ _ from ha)
  exact h

/-- **The canonical map lands in the inverse-image ideal sheaf, over an arbitrary open.**
Membership is local, and every point has a compatible pair of affine charts around it. -/
theorem pullbackIdealMap_app_mem_opens (W : X.Opens)
    (s : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj
      (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules), W)) :
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (pullbackIdealMap q I) W s ∈
      ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op W) := by
  refine mem_submodule_of_cover _ W _ (fun x hx => ?_)
  obtain ⟨U, V, hVW, hxV, hVU⟩ := exists_affine_chart_pair q W x hx
  refine ⟨V.1, hxV, hVW, ?_⟩
  have h := pullbackIdealMap_app_mem q I U V hVU
    (((Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj
      (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules)).presheaf.map (homOfLE hVW).op s)
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_presheaf_map] at h
  exact h

/-- **The canonical map is onto the inverse-image ideal sheaf, over a pair of affine charts.**
The ideal `(I.comap q)(V)` is generated by the images of the sections of `I` over `U`
(`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`), each generator is hit by the pullback of the
corresponding section, and the set of values of the map on sections is a submodule. -/
theorem exists_app_eq_of_mem (U : Y.affineOpens) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (hVU : (V : X.Opens) ≤ q ⁻¹ᵁ (U : Y.Opens))
    (t : Γ(Scheme.unitModule X, V.1))
    (ht : t ∈ ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.obj (op V.1)) :
    ∃ s, Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (pullbackIdealMap q I) V.1 s = t := by
  rw [comap_unitSubmodule_obj_eq_map q I U V hVU] at ht
  have key := Submodule.span_le (R := Γ(X, V.1)) (M := Γ(X.unitModule, V.1))
    (p := LinearMap.range (appLinear (pullbackIdealMap q I) V.1))
    (s := (q.appLE U.1 V.1 hVU).hom '' (I.ideal U : Set Γ(Y, U.1)))
  refine key.2 ?_ ht
  rintro _ ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
  have ha' : a ∈ I.unitSubmodule.toSubmodule.obj (op U.1) := by
    rwa [AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.unitSubmodule_obj_affine]
  exact ⟨pullbackSect q (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) U.1 V.1 hVU ⟨a, ha'⟩,
    pullbackIdealMap_app_pullbackSect q I U.1 V.1 hVU ⟨a, ha'⟩⟩

/-! ### The comparison -/

/-- **The comparison map `q^* I ⟶ I.comap q`**: the factorisation of the canonical map
`q^* I ⟶ 𝒪_X` through the ideal sheaf of the inverse image. -/
def pullbackIdealComparison :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) ⟶
      (((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSheafOfModules : X.Modules) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.liftToSubmodule (pullbackIdealMap q I) ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule)
    (pullbackIdealMap_app_mem_opens q I)

/-- The comparison map is compatible with the inclusion of the inverse-image ideal sheaf into
the structure sheaf: that is what identifies it. -/
theorem pullbackIdealComparison_comp_iota :
    pullbackIdealComparison q I ≫ idealIota (I.comap q) = pullbackIdealMap q I := rfl

/-- **The comparison map is a monomorphism when `q` is flat.** The inclusion `I ⟶ 𝒪_Y` is a
monomorphism and the pullback along a flat morphism preserves monomorphisms, so the canonical
map `q^* I ⟶ 𝒪_X` is one; the comparison is a factor of it. -/
instance mono_pullbackIdealComparison [AlgebraicGeometry.Flat q] :
    Mono (C := X.Modules) (pullbackIdealComparison q I) := by
  have h1 : Mono (C := X.Modules) (pullbackIdealMap q I) := by
    rw [pullbackIdealMap]
    exact @mono_comp _ _ _ _ _ _
      (Scheme.Modules.mono_pullback_map_of_flat q (idealIota I)
        (Stacks.Algebraization.monoSubmoduleι I.unitSubmodule)) _ inferInstance
  rw [← pullbackIdealComparison_comp_iota q I] at h1
  exact mono_of_mono _ (idealIota (I.comap q))

/-- **The comparison map is an epimorphism**, with no hypothesis on `q`. Epimorphy of a morphism
of sheaves of modules is local surjectivity, and on a compatible pair of affine charts the map on
sections is onto by `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.exists_app_eq_of_mem`. -/
instance epi_pullbackIdealComparison : Epi (C := X.Modules) (pullbackIdealComparison q I) := by
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _ ?_
  constructor
  intro W t
  rw [Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨U, V, hVW, hxV, hVU⟩ := exists_affine_chart_pair q W x hx
  refine ⟨V.1, homOfLE hVW, ?_, hxV⟩
  have hmem := ((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSubmodule.map_mem (homOfLE hVW).op t.2
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_app_eq_of_mem q I U V hVU _ hmem
  exact ⟨s, Subtype.ext hs⟩

/-- **The comparison map is invertible when `q` is flat**: it is a monomorphism and an
epimorphism in an abelian category. -/
instance isIso_pullbackIdealComparison [AlgebraicGeometry.Flat q] :
    IsIso (C := X.Modules) (pullbackIdealComparison q I) :=
  isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-- **Flat base change for the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme.** For a flat morphism of
schemes `q : X ⟶ Y` and a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `I` on `Y`, the pullback of the ideal
sheaf of `I` is the ideal sheaf of the inverse image `I.comap q`:

`q^* (I ⊆ 𝒪_Y) ≅ (I·𝒪_X ⊆ 𝒪_X)`. -/
def pullbackIdealFlatIso [AlgebraicGeometry.Flat q] :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback q).obj (I.unitSubmodule.toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) ≅
      (((I.comap q).unitSubmodule).toSheafOfModules : X.Modules) :=
  asIso (C := X.Modules) (pullbackIdealComparison q I)

/-- Under `Stacks.ClosedSubscheme.pullbackIdealFlatIso` the inclusion of the inverse-image ideal
sheaf into `𝒪_X` pulls back to the pullback of the inclusion of `I` into `𝒪_Y`. This pins the
isomorphism down: it is a map of subsheaves of the structure sheaf, not merely an abstract
identification. -/
theorem pullbackIdealFlatIso_hom_comp_iota [AlgebraicGeometry.Flat q] :
    (pullbackIdealFlatIso q I).hom ≫ idealIota (I.comap q) = pullbackIdealMap q I := rfl

end Stacks.ClosedSubscheme

end
